  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "Which of the following is equal to \\[\\dfrac{\\frac13-\\frac14\\ }{\\ \\frac12-\\frac13\\ }?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac14\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac13\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac12\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac23\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac34\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "First simplify the numerator and denominator separately, using common denominators:\n\\[\n\\frac13-\\frac14=\\frac4{12}-\\frac3{12}=\\frac1{12},\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac12-\\frac13=\\frac36-\\frac26=\\frac16.\n\\]\nThe denominator is nonzero, so we can divide by multiplying by its reciprocal:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\frac1{12}}{\\frac16}\n=\\frac1{12}\\cdot6\n=\\boxed{\\frac12}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
